  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe primary approach involves refining the optimization process to better explore the search space and avoid local optima. The core idea is to use a combination of informed initial guesses, advanced optimization techniques, and dynamic perturbations to iteratively improve the solution. By increasing the number of clusters and using more sophisticated perturbation strategies, the algorithm can better distribute the mass of h(x) to minimize overlap. This addresses the bottleneck of local optima by introducing variability in initialization and exploration.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nThe representation uses a step function h(x) with n_points samples on [0, 2], satisfying:\n- 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n- \u2211h[i] = n_points / 2\n\nThe objective is to minimize:\nC\u2085 = max_k [\u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx] * dx\n\nWhere dx = 2.0 / n_points. Constraints are enforced via:\n- A hard constraint \u2211h[i] = n_points / 2\n- Bounds 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n\nThe optimization uses a hybrid of SLSQP and L-BFGS-B with random restarts, ensuring constraint satisfaction through rescaling after clipping.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na) Input: n_points = 400, initial_h_values (if available)\nb) Generate initial clusters:\n   - If initial_h_values exists, use it as base\n   - Else, create 6 clusters with uniform spacing and variable widths\nc) Optimization loop:\n   - Perform 500 iterations of:\n      i) SLSQP with bounds and constraint\n      ii) Perturb solution with noise \u00b10.05\n      iii) Apply rescaling to maintain integral\nd) Track best solution via:\n   - Evaluate objective after each iteration\n   - Retain solution with lowest C\u2085\ne) Final refinement:\n   - Apply L-BFGS-B for 50 iterations on best candidate\nf) Output: best_h.tolist(), best_c5, n_points\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\nDefault configuration:\n- n_clusters = 6\n- Noise amplitude = 0.05\n- Iterations = 500\n- Refinement steps = 50\n\nVariations:\n- Cluster count: 4, 6, 8\n- Noise amplitude: 0.02-0.1\n- Optimization method: SLSQP vs L-BFGS-B\n- Perturbation frequency: 0.1 probability per iteration\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nTime allocation:\n- 90% for optimization loop\n- 10% for refinement\n\nTermination checks:\n- After 500 iterations (150s)\n- If improvement stalls for 30 iterations, force termination\n\nFallback:\n- If initial_h_values exists, use it as baseline\n- If no valid candidate, return initial_h_values\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nChecks:\n- All h[i] \u2208 [0,1] (via clipping)\n- \u2211h = n_points / 2 (via rescaling)\n- Objective evaluation matches np.correlate with full mode\n\nRe-evaluation:\n- Final candidate re-evaluated with exact evaluator\n- Sanity check: max lag overlap \u2264 0.38085",
